cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference VAJRA in academic or policy work, please cite it as below."
title: "VAJRA: A Zero-Trust Cryptographic Architecture for High-Stakes Examination Distribution"
abstract: >
  VAJRA is a prototype cryptographic architecture for examination paper
  distribution that makes pre-exam leaks mathematically impossible. It
  composes three independent locks — a Rivest-Shamir-Wagner sequential
  time-lock puzzle, k-of-n Shamir secret sharing across regional centres,
  and per-centre X25519 hybrid encryption — with a drand distributed
  randomness beacon as a publicly verifiable wall-clock anchor. The
  decryption ceremony is decentralized: no single party, including the
  administrator, holds enough information to recover the exam paper
  before the configured exam-start moment, and cooperation from a
  threshold of independent centres is required even then.
